TITLE:: Arranger
SUMMARY:: Absolute layout of sequence chips for the SequencerGui Arrange page.
CATEGORIES:: Streams-Patterns-Events
RELATED:: Classes/PatternChip, Classes/SCViewHolder, Classes/Sequencer, Classes/SequencerDocument, Classes/SequencerGui

DESCRIPTION::
TELETYPE::Arranger:: is a LINK::Classes/SCViewHolder:: that LINK::Classes/SequencerGui:: shows when the Arrange button is pressed. Its view has no layout decorator, so each LINK::Classes/PatternChip:: keeps the bounds it is given. A chip whose id has a stored origin is pinned there. The other chips pack in LINK::Classes/Sequencer#-sequenceIds:: order, with a margin of 10 and a gap of 10, wrapping to the arranger's width. Resizing packs only the unpinned chips and clamps pinned chips into the view for display. That clamp is not written. Dropping a dragged chip stores the clamped integer origin and, when a LINK::Classes/SequencerDocument:: was given, writes the origin map. A CODE::nil:: document skips the write.

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: new
Creates an instance of TELETYPE::Arranger::.

ARGUMENT:: sequencer
The LINK::Classes/Sequencer:: whose sequences this arranger lists and plays.

ARGUMENT:: sequencerDocument
The LINK::Classes/SequencerDocument:: that receives chip origins on drop, or CODE::nil:: when there is nothing to write.

RETURNS::
A new TELETYPE::Arranger:: instance.

INSTANCEMETHODS::

METHOD:: addSequence
Adds a chip for CODE::name::. A name that is already shown is left as it is. A stored origin pins the chip. Otherwise the chip is packed with the other unpinned chips.

ARGUMENT:: name
A LINK::Classes/Symbol::, displayed with CODE::asString::.

METHOD:: applyOrigins
Moves each shown chip to its stored origin and pins it. A chip with no stored origin becomes unpinned and is packed again. This does not write the document.

PRIVATE:: init, prClamp, prClampPinned, prCommitDrag, prPackUnpinned, prPlaceChip, prViewReady
